# Repo-wide .dockerignore.
#
# Pre-#490 the repo had no .dockerignore, so every `docker compose
# build` shipped the full 33 GB working tree (24 GB of bags, 4.4 GB
# of UE5 build artifacts, 1.4 GB of .git) through Docker Desktop's
# 9p/virtiofs mount as build context — on Windows + WSL2 with the
# repo on /mnt/c that was the dominant cost of an image build
# (~minutes), even when the actual COPY in the Dockerfile only
# needed ~50 MB of source.
#
# Allowlist would be cleaner but Docker BuildKit's exclusion semantics
# don't compose well with multi-stage `COPY` from different paths,
# and we'd risk silently dropping a path some Dockerfile depends on.
# So this is a denylist: exclude the obvious heavyweight stuff that
# no Dockerfile in this repo COPYs from. Audit point: when adding a
# new Dockerfile, check what it COPYs and verify nothing here would
# hide it.
#
# Cost dropped from ~33 GB → ~200 MB after this file. On Windows
# /mnt/c that takes the build-context transfer from minutes to seconds.

# ---- VCS ----
.git
.gitattributes
.gitmodules
# Nested .git — the pipeline/ submodule has a .git gitlink file that
# `COPY pipeline/ src/` would otherwise drop into the colcon workspace.
**/.git
# The pipeline submodule ships its own README at its root; it's not a
# ROS package so colcon ignores it, but keep it out of the image src/.
pipeline/README.md

# ---- UE5 build/cooked output (5+ GB combined) ----
# Saved/ holds StagedBuilds (the packaged .app), logs, AutoSaves,
# editor crashdumps. Intermediate/ is UE5's transient build dir.
# DerivedDataCache/ is GiB-scale; cooked Saved/Cooked/ likewise.
# None of this is consumed by any Dockerfile.
Saved
Intermediate
DerivedDataCache
Binaries
Build

# ---- UE5 content (binary .uasset / .umap; multi-GB) ----
# Tracks ARE bind-mounted into mc_backend at runtime (UE5 host
# process needs the same dir for loadTrack) — but we never COPY
# them into an image, so they're safe to exclude from build context.
Content

# ---- Bag recordings (#465; 24 GB on a busy dev box) ----
# Bags land in the `ifssim_bags` named volume per #490, but the
# host-side `bags/` directory still holds historical recordings
# pulled via tools/pull-bag.sh. Image builds never need any of it.
bags

# ---- Plugin build artifacts ----
Plugins/*/Binaries
Plugins/*/Intermediate
Plugins/*/Saved
# Plugin source ITSELF (Plugins/*/Source) IS sometimes COPY'd into
# images that build the C++ bridge against it — don't exclude that.

# ---- Editor / IDE / OS junk ----
.vscode
.idea
*.user
*.suo
*.opensdf
*.sdf
.vs
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# ---- Node / frontend ----
# mc_frontend's Dockerfile installs node_modules INSIDE the image
# from package.json — host node_modules is wasted context. Same for
# any random-track-generator dev installs.
node_modules
npm-debug.log
.next
.turbo
.parcel-cache

# ---- Python ----
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
.tox
.venv
venv
*.egg-info

# ---- ROS / colcon ----
# Local colcon trees from running tests on the host; in-container
# builds happen fresh inside the Dockerfile.
build
install
log

# ---- Docker / compose artifacts ----
# Anything we'd want to keep is committed under docker/.
docker-compose.override.yml
.env

# ---- Misc large binary outputs ----
dist
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.tar.bz2
*.7z
*.mcap
*.bag
*.db3

# ---- Documentation builds ----
docs/_build
docs/_site
site

ifs-onboarding
